# Context

## Background
Hosted CI exposed two portability differences not visible under the development stable toolchain: Clippy 1.97 rejects a redundant formatting borrow, and musl does not export renameat2 as a linkable libc symbol.

## Why This Way
Linux atomic no-replace now invokes SYS_renameat2 directly through libc::syscall. This preserves the same kernel primitive and RENAME_NOREPLACE semantics across glibc and musl without adding a dependency or falling back to a racy existence check.

## Verification
The complete local suite, Rust 1.82 check, and x86_64-unknown-linux-musl release link passed before push.
